2","idp_filedate":1792410771000,"nhcTitle":"Off the East Coast of the United States","discussion":"A storm-force non-tropical low pressure area is located along a  frontal boundary a few hundred miles off the southeast coast of the  United States. This low is likely to move slowly and erratically  over the next couple of days. If the low remains over the Gulf  Stream and becomes detached from the front, it could briefly acquire  some subtropical cyclone characteristics during the middle to latter  portions of the week. The system is expected to begin to move  northeastward away from the the eastern United States later this  week, and environmental conditions are expected to become  unfavorable for development by the weekend.  Regardless of the  status of the system, high winds, coastal flooding, and dangerous  surf are expected along portions of the U.S. East Coast during the  next few days. Please consult statements and warnings from local  National Weather Service offices and the Weather Prediction Center  for more information, along with High Seas Forecasts and Storm  Warnings issued by the National Weather Service. \n Formation chance through 48 hours...low...near 0 percent. \n Formation chance through 7 days...medium...40 percent.","disturbance":1}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-93.34022372635525,6.13168396282502],[-93.13617840741458,6.1444530347580555],[-92.93817441808285,6.159479905218385],[-92.74615845541214,6.176754864692698],[-92.56007721645447,6.1962682036676835],[-92.3798773982619,6.218010212630032],[-92.20550569788641,6.241971182066432],[-92.0369088123801,6.26814140246357],[-91.87403343879498,6.29651116430814],[-91.71682627418309,6.327070758086829],[-91.56523401559646,6.359810474286326],[-91.41920336008715,6.394720603393321],[-91.27868100470718,6.431791435894502],[-91.14361364650861,6.471013262276561],[-91.01394798254344,6.512376373026184],[-90.88963070986374,6.555871058630061],[-90.77060852552151,6.601487609574882],[-